content.text:
The evidence is consistent: one fault, a profile pod that is gone for the whole abnormal window. Its failure reaches the user through the frontend.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "profile",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT 'normal' AS period, service_name, attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, count(*) AS n, min(time) AS first_ts, max(time) AS last_ts FROM normal_metrics_sum WHERE service_name = 'profile' GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'abnormal', service_name, attr_k8s_pod_name, count(*), min(time), max(time) FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE service_name = 'profile' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Profile pod emits uptime/metrics in the normal period, and has no metric rows at all in the abnormal window."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, count(*) AS spans FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'profile' GROUP BY service_name",
          "claim": "Profile service produces zero spans in the abnormal window, versus about 1,163 server spans per period in normal."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT attr_status_code, count(*) AS n, round(avg(duration)/1e6, 3) AS avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name = 'profile.Profile/GetProfiles' GROUP BY attr_status_code",
          "claim": "Frontend's GetProfiles calls to profile all fail with Error status in about 0.01 ms, versus about 2 ms normally."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, message, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE message = 'Get profiles failed' GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "Frontend logs about 1,627 ERROR 'Get profiles failed' entries in the abnormal window; normal period has none."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "profile",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "WITH r AS (SELECT trace_id FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name = 'HTTP /recommendations' AND attr_http_response_status_code = 500 LIMIT 1) SELECT s.span_name, s.service_name, s.attr_span_kind, s.attr_status_code, round(s.duration/1e6, 3) AS ms FROM abnormal_traces s JOIN r ON s.trace_id = r.trace_id ORDER BY s.time",
          "claim": "A failing /recommendations request: recommendation succeeds, then frontend's profile GetProfiles call errors and the frontend returns 500."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

